{"t": 1794119986.8366375, "kind": "call", "tool": "slack_post_message", "args": {"channel_id": "C07INCID003", "text": "reports-api 502 \u2014 root cause found, patch ready\n\nCause: CloudWatch logs (/ecs/reports-api, eu-west-1) show every export failing with `ValueError: dict contains fields not in fieldnames: 'currency'`. Upstream ledger 2026.11 added a `currency` field to every row, but reports/export.py only declared `id` and `amount`, so the export handler raised on every request and the API answered 502.\n\nFix: reports/export.py now exports `id,amount,currency` and ignores unknown extra fields. Verified locally against new rows (with currency) and legacy rows (without).\n\nNext: deploy reports-api, then confirm export requests return 200."}, "ok": true}
